1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,500
YOU'RE GIVING HER THAT? OVER THE SOAP THING?

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:06,700
JADA. WE TALKED ABOUT THIS.

3
00:00:06,700 --> 00:00:08,400
TALKED ABOUT WHAT?

4
00:00:09,800 --> 00:00:12,300
YOU'RE PUTTING ME IN A HOME?

5
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:15,600
MAMA. WE WERE GONNA WAIT TILL AFTER CAKE.

6
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:17,200
ON MY BIRTHDAY?

7
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:22,100
SOAP. YOU THINK I CAN'T RINSE A POT?

8
00:00:22,100 --> 00:00:25,000
EVERY DINNER SINCE CHRISTMAS. WE'VE ALL NOTICED.

9
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:26,700
ALL OF YOU?

10
00:00:26,700 --> 00:00:29,500
TASTE BUDS GO AS YOU GET OLDER.

11
00:00:29,500 --> 00:00:34,400
BUT IF YOU CAN'T TASTE SOAP, WHAT HAPPENS WHEN YOU CAN'T SMELL GAS?

12
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:38,000
I'VE COOKED IN THIS KITCHEN FOR FORTY-TWO YEARS.

13
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:42,400
I KNOW. THAT'S WHY I DON'T WANT YOU IN IT ALONE.

14
00:00:42,400 --> 00:00:47,000
WRENFIELD HAS A UNIT OPENING THIS MONTH. I PUT DOWN A DEPOSIT.

15
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:48,800
YOU ALREADY PAID?

16
00:00:48,800 --> 00:00:51,800
NO, SHE WON'T FIGHT IT. SHE'S — SLIPPING.

17
00:00:54,700 --> 00:00:56,500
GRANDMA, IT'S STILL THERE.

18
00:00:56,500 --> 00:01:00,600
I SCRUBBED THAT PAN THREE TIMES. NEW SOAP. NEW SPONGE.

19
00:01:00,600 --> 00:01:03,100
AND I CAN'T TASTE A THING.

20
00:01:03,100 --> 00:01:05,500
JADA, AM I LOSING IT?

21
00:01:06,900 --> 00:01:08,900
I LOVE YOU, GRANDMA.

22
00:01:12,300 --> 00:01:15,500
WASN'T SHE THE ONE PUSHING YOU INTO WRENFIELD?

23
00:01:15,500 --> 00:01:16,800
SHE SURE WAS.

24
00:01:16,800 --> 00:01:20,800
NOW SHE'S HERE EVERY SUNDAY, TAKING PLATES HOME. WHAT CHANGED?

25
00:01:20,800 --> 00:01:24,100
SHE TOLD ME MY COOKING TASTED LIKE SOAP.

26
00:01:25,100 --> 00:01:26,500
MINE TOO.

27
00:01:26,500 --> 00:01:28,300
SHOW ME YOUR KITCHEN.

28
00:01:28,300 --> 00:01:30,000
WHEN'D YOU BUY THESE?

29
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:34,000
AFTER THANKSGIVING. TERRANCE SENT ME AN ARTICLE ABOUT BLACK PLASTIC.

30
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:36,500
AND WHEN DID THE SOAP START?

31
00:01:37,500 --> 00:01:38,800
CHRISTMAS.

32
00:01:38,800 --> 00:01:40,000
SMELL IT.

33
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:41,800
THAT'S MY DISH SOAP.

34
00:01:41,800 --> 00:01:44,600
IT SOAKS UP WHATEVER SOAP YOU USE.

35
00:01:44,600 --> 00:01:47,800
THE MINUTE IT GETS HOT, OUT IT COMES.

36
00:01:47,800 --> 00:01:49,900
BUT I CAN'T TASTE IT.

37
00:01:49,900 --> 00:01:53,500
NEITHER COULD I. COOK'S ALWAYS THE LAST TO NOTICE.

38
00:01:53,500 --> 00:01:57,700
THEY TESTED SILICONE BAKING PANS. IN THE OVEN, CHEMICALS LEACHED OUT.

39
00:01:57,700 --> 00:02:01,000
SOME OF THEM ARE LINKED TO HORMONE DISRUPTION.

40
00:02:02,900 --> 00:02:06,000
I THREW ALL MINE OUT AND GOT THESE.

41
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:09,200
WOOD? THE CHEAP ONES BLEED IN THE POT.

42
00:02:09,200 --> 00:02:11,600
THAT'S THE FINISH, NOT THE WOOD.

43
00:02:11,600 --> 00:02:16,300
EVERY PIECE IS ONE BLOCK OF WOOD. NO GLUE. NOTHING PAINTED ON.

44
00:02:16,300 --> 00:02:19,900
THEY'RE CALLED ACAWOOD. I JUST TEXTED YOU THE LINK.

45
00:02:22,300 --> 00:02:24,500
KEEP THESE TILL YOURS COME.

46
00:02:24,500 --> 00:02:26,900
MOVERS COME SATURDAY AT NINE, MAMA.

47
00:02:26,900 --> 00:02:28,200
SMELL THIS FIRST.

48
00:02:28,300 --> 00:02:30,800
MAMA. THIS ISN'T ABOUT A SPATULA.

49
00:02:30,800 --> 00:02:32,200
SMELL IT, TERRANCE.

50
00:02:33,400 --> 00:02:34,800
THAT'S DISH SOAP.

51
00:02:34,900 --> 00:02:38,100
NOW DOROTHY'S. SHE COOKS WITH IT EVERY DAY.

52
00:02:38,100 --> 00:02:39,300
NOTHING.

53
00:02:39,300 --> 00:02:41,800
ONE SNIFF. MY NOSE IS FINE.

54
00:02:41,800 --> 00:02:45,000
YOU'RE THE ONE WHO SENT ME THAT ARTICLE.

55
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:47,600
SMELLING'S ONE THING, MAMA. TASTING'S ANOTHER.

56
00:02:47,600 --> 00:02:51,200
FRIDAY NIGHT, I'M MAKING MY POTATO SALAD. EVERYBODY COMES.

57
00:02:51,200 --> 00:02:56,900
IF ANYBODY TASTES SOAP, I'LL GET IN YOUR CAR SATURDAY AND NEVER SAY A WORD.

58
00:02:56,900 --> 00:02:58,200
DEAL.

59
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:03,100
JADA. YOU FIRST. YOU'RE THE HONEST ONE.

60
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:06,200
GRANDMA.

61
00:03:06,200 --> 00:03:08,100
THERE'S NO SOAP. NONE.

62
00:03:09,700 --> 00:03:11,700
MAMA. I'M SO SORRY.

63
00:03:13,300 --> 00:03:15,100
UNPACK MY BOWLS, TERRANCE.

64
00:03:15,100 --> 00:03:16,200
SECONDS?

65
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:22,700
MY SON ALMOST MOVED ME OUT OF MY OWN KITCHEN. OVER THIS.

66
00:03:22,700 --> 00:03:26,900
BEFORE ANYBODY TELLS YOU YOU'VE LOST YOUR TOUCH, SMELL YOUR SPATULA.

67
00:03:26,900 --> 00:03:30,800
IF IT SMELLS LIKE DISH SOAP, SO DOES YOUR DINNER.

68
00:03:30,800 --> 00:03:36,500
AND IF IT'S YOUR WIFE'S COOKING, OR YOUR MAMA'S? SMELL HERS BEFORE YOU BLAME HER.

69
00:03:36,500 --> 00:03:42,200
MINE ARE ACAWOOD NOW. SEVEN PIECES, EACH ONE CUT FROM A SINGLE BLOCK OF WOOD.

70
00:03:42,200 --> 00:03:47,700
NOTHING ON THEM BUT OIL OR WAX. HERE'S ONE IN HOT WATER. STILL CLEAR.

71
00:03:47,700 --> 00:03:49,400
HAND WASH, DRY, DONE.

72
00:03:49,500 --> 00:03:55,900
EIGHTY-NINE NINETY-FIVE WITH THE HOLDER. FREE SHIPPING IN THE U.S., AND NINETY-DAY RETURNS.

73
00:03:55,900 --> 00:03:59,800
THE LINK'S RIGHT BELOW. AND MY KITCHEN? STILL MINE.

